Package: martinmunk-avr-controld
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.11)
Description: broker daemon for AV receivers (serial/telnet), socket API, MQTT
 avr-controld owns the one connection to an AV receiver (NAD, Opalum, ...) and
 serves it to the ALSA volume plugins, the HDMI-CEC relay and an AirPlay power
 policy over a Unix socket, and optionally to Home Assistant as MQTT entities
 (power/volume/mute/input and every extra the receiver exposes). It ships all
 Python dependencies (nad-receiver, opalum-receiver, paho-mqtt, pyserial,
 jeepney) as a private library tree under /opt/avr-controld/lib, run by the
 system python3, so nothing is pulled from PyPI on the target and everything
 stays dpkg-tracked.
